[[File:S1E02 DeFoe Grier.jpg|thumb|170px|DeFoe sends his men to find [[Eathon Lambert's journal]]]]
Little is known about DeFoe's background, but his rocket-like rise through [[the Organization]] hierarchy is legendary amongst [[Suits]]. Within a matter of months, DeFoe was promoted through Suit rankings to be a prominent leader of his own squad. {{source|Huntik.com}}

Under the Professor, one of DeFoe's earlier missions was to retrieve [[Eathon Lambert's journal]], although the mission ended with the journal being all but destroyed. {{source|A Seeker Is Born}} DeFoe then ordered [[Grier]] to find the biggest [[Venice Huntik Library]] because he knew that the Huntik team needed to research [[Eathon Lambert|Eathon]]'s journal. DeFoe later attacked the library, breaking through by pouring acid on the door's knob. Though he failed to retrieve the journal he manages to learn the Huntik team's next move. {{Source|The Casterwill Client}}

After DeFoe learned that the Huntik team is going to [[Prague, Czech Republic]], to get the Titan [[Metagolem]] he ambushed the Huntik team when they were going to retrieve the [[Jodis Lore's Key]], He successfully obtained the key and went to the [[Golem's Attic]], Where he tried to bond with the Titan Metagolem but failed due to [[Dante]]'s interference so DeFoe retreated because Dante had bonded with Metagolem. {{Source|Words of Truth, Heart of Lies}}
[[File:S1E04 Defoe bonded.jpg|thumb|170px|DeFoe finds the Amulet of [[Gar-Ghoul]]]]
Afterwards, DeFoe's team was sent to retrieve the [[Amulets]] of the re-awakening [[Titans]]. In the [[Cave of the Gargoyle]] on the outskirts of [[Rouen, France]], DeFoe managed to retrieve and bond with [[Gar-Ghoul]]. {{source|Into the River of Secrets}}. DeFoe then was ordered by [[the Professor]] to retrieve the [[Ring of Arc]]. He then had a rematch between [[Dante]]'s [[Caliban]] and DeFoe's "new friend," his [[Gar-Ghoul]], but Dante fled with the other's to the catacombs. {{Source|Crawling the Catacombs}} DeFoe pursued the team, intent on obtaining the [[Ring of Arc]], but failed due to [[Dante]]'s plan, dividing up his forces and sneaking the Ring past them using [[Gareon]]. Because of this failure, he was removed from his duties, by [[Rassimov]] as [[the Professor]] was too furious to lay eyes on him. DeFoe then swore to bring [[Dante]]'s end with or without [[the Organization]]. {{Source|Divide and Conquer}}
[[File:S1E10 Defoe Dante.jpg|thumb|170px|DeFoe has a final showdown with Dante]]
His removal was temporary, as he was later reinstated by [[Rassimov]] after nearly destroying the Organization's training machine while training. DeFoe was then given a mission to retrieve the Amulet of [[King Basilisk]], but he again failed due to the intervention of Dante's team. {{Source|Absent Heroes}}

DeFoe was then ordered simply to deliver the [[Sword of Saint George]] to [[Prague, Czech Republic]]. The Sword contained the Titan [[Lindorm]], but the Organization considered DeFoe to be unworthy to bond with the Titan. Unsatisfied at simply being a "delivery boy," he went to Greece after receiving word from his spies that Dante Vale was sighted there in order to kill Dante. DeFoe, however, failed, resulting in Lok bonding with Lindorm and DeFoe's Amulets being taken by the [[Huntik Foundation]]. {{source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}} 
[[File:S1E11 Grier kills Defoe.jpg|thumb|170px|DeFoe is killed by his own right-hand man, [[Grier]]]]
Having been removed from his duties, DeFoe planned to to use his operative access to steal a number of Titans from the Organization for his revenge on Dante Vale. However, he was murdered by his own right-hand man, Grier, by order of [[the Professor]], who thought Defoe to be incapable of carrying out his orders.{{source|The Beautiful Trap}} 

Whilst attempting to reason with [[Wilder]], Sophie told him she had thought him to be different from DeFoe or [[Klaus]], because of his talk of uniting people, to which Wilder said they were just "protecting the status quo". Grier later implied his killing of DeFoe to be a reason for him to stay on [[Sutos Island]] and not join the [[Huntik Foundation]], telling Dante that he had done a lot of things that he was not proud of to reach his position. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}

